  abstract = {The purpose of this study sought to gauge student-athlete opinions on impending Name, Image, and Likeness NCAA legislation. The study asked student-athletes a variety of questions on NIL compensation in addition to gaining qualitative data on their thoughts, concerns, and opinions. Findings point to a general support of NIL compensation among student-athletes along with concerns surrounding, gender equity, non-revenue v. revenue disparity, and maintaining a focus on priorities. A majority of respondents expressed a desire for more understanding or knowledge surrounding the subject. Responses differed significantly among gender, athlete type, and grade level. These and other findings, and their implications for NCAA policy and pending litigation related to student-athlete NIL compensation, are discussed. Recommendations include clarification and focused rules’ education for student-athletes, as well as discussions surrounding possible implications for specific groups of student-athletes.},
