  abstract = {If conservatives are to win elections then they will need to stop blaming others for the predicaments in which they find themselves and start having respect for the common sense of the American people. This means doing what is right politically, within a constitutional framework and in line with deeply held principles, to achieve electoral majorities. The liberals do not understand this concept, but they are fortunate to have a leader who does and who uses his power to force the Democratic Party to pay attention to the voice of the people. President Bill Clinton's term in office has been the most flawed of the 20th century and he has been at the center of the worst White House scandal since Watergate, but he has been able mold his party, both tactically and ideologically, into a far more sensible faction. Conservatives complain at this state of affairs, but they should be asking themselves how Clinton and the Left manages to do it. Clinton is able to claim to stand for the dispossessed in society, and conservatives will continue to lose elections until they remove this weapon from the Democratic arsenal.},
