  abstract = {PERCEPTIONS OF THE SIMILARITY OF COUNTRIES WERE ANALYZED BY FACTOR ANALYSIS AND SMALLEST SPACE ANALYSIS. THE TASK FOR THE RESPONDENTS INVOLVED PICKING THOSE 3 COUNTRIES FROM A LIST OF 16 NATIONS WHICH WERE MOST SIMILAR TO AN ANCHOR COUNTRY. 2 SETS OF RESPONDENTS COMPLETED THIS TASK: A RANDOM PROBABILITY SAMPLE OF 557 ADULTS AND 148 FACULTY MEMBERS. FOR THE PUBLIC SAMPLE, THE MAJOR FACTOR IN THE PERCEPTUAL SPACE WAS COMMUNISM, WITH ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT, SPANISH INFLUENCE, AND EUROPE VS. ASIA APPEARING NEXT IN ORDER OF IMPORTANCE. ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT PREDOMINATED IN THE ANALYSIS OF ACADEMIC PERCEPTIONS, WITH SPANISH INFLUENCE, COMMUNISM, AND AFRICA VS. ASIA IN THAT ORDER AS THE REMAINING FACTORS. INTERPRETATION OF THE FACTORS WAS SUBSTANTIATED BY HIGH CORRELATIONS BETWEEN RESPONDENT RATINGS OF NATIONS ON CONCEPTS REPRESENTING THESE FACTORS AND THE FACTOR LOADINGS THEMSELVES.(15 REF.) (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)},
