  abstract = {In keeping with traditionalsociological concerns about orderand disorder, this essay addresses the dark side of organizations. To build a theoretical basis forthe darkside as an integratedfield of study,I review fourliteratures in orderto make core ideas of each availableto specialists in the others.Using a Simmelian-basedcase comparisonmethod of analogical theorizing,I first consider sociological constructsthat identify both the generic social form andthe generic origin of routinenonconformity:how things go wrong in socially organizedsettings.ThenI examinethreetypes of routinenonconformity with adverse outcomes that harmthe public: mistake, misconduct, and disasterproducedin andby organizations.Searchingfor analogies and differences,I find thatin common,routinenonconformity,mistake,misconduct,anddisasteraresystematicallyproducedby the interconnectionbetween environment,organizations,cognition, and choice. These patternsamplify what is known about social structureand have implications for theory, research, and policy.},
